378:## Slice 18: Ayula, Queen Among Bears
379:Ayula is a supported commander (`{1}{G}`, 2/2 Legendary Bear) with sourced printing data in `fixtures/starter-corpus/slice18-sourced.json`. Her trigger fires only for another Bear its controller controls; token entries count and opposing Bear entries do not. The controller chooses counters or fight before targets. Counters may target any Bear (including an opponent's). Fight requires a Bear you control and a creature you don't control, revalidates both at resolution, and deals damage simultaneously through the existing prevention/replacement pipeline. Ayula has 29 missing desired-list cards after slice 19; the eight-list gate remains open.
382:`Spectral Bears` (`{1}{G}` Creature — Bear Spirit 3/3, me1 131, sourced in `fixtures/starter-corpus/slice19-sourced.json`) is the pool's first attack trigger. Its printed intervening-if — "if defending player controls no black nontoken permanents" — is evaluated in the declare attackers step before the trigger is queued and again at resolution, so an attack into a black nontoken permanent never reaches the stack, while a black *token* does not satisfy the exclusion. The payoff marks the attacker so that its controller's next untap step leaves it tapped exactly once (CR 502.3); the marker is serde-skipped when empty, so every previously recorded digest is unchanged. Black is read from the printed mana cost (CR 202.2a) or the token's own colors. Attack triggers are now infrastructure rather than a card patch: `TriggerEvent::Attacks` plus `TriggerCondition`, the latter evaluated before queueing and re-checked at resolution. Ayula has 29 missing names; the eight-list gate remains open and no list is certified by this slice.
